  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "The tangent to a curve with $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=2x-4$ makes an angle of inclination of $135^\\circ$ with the $x$-axis at the point $(2,-4)$. Find its equation.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac{x^3}{3}-2x^2+3x-\\frac{14}{3}$",
      "worked": "The angle of inclination gives the gradient $\\tan135^\\circ=-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y'&=x^2-4x+C_1\\\\-1&=2^2-4(2)+C_1\\\\-1&=4-8+C_1\\\\C_1&=3\\\\y'&=x^2-4x+3\\\\y&=\\frac{x^3}{3}-2x^2+3x+C_2\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstitute $(2,-4)$:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}-4&=\\frac{2^3}{3}-2(2)^2+3(2)+C_2\\\\-4&=\\frac{8}{3}-8+6+C_2\\\\C_2&=-\\frac{14}{3}\\\\y&=\\frac{x^3}{3}-2x^2+3x-\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 59
  },
